{"base_rate":0.013636363636363636,"brier":0.014673484848484849,"bss":-0.09093189964157711,"bss_hi":NaN,"bss_lo":NaN,"chart":{"base":[79.7,251.0],"lead":"62,252.4 272,228.3 482,205.4 692,201.6","note":{"base":"skill -0.09 — higher than 3% of cities","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 61% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 1%; promised 2% → rained 1%"},"rel":"75.4,460.1"},"country":"AE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.007681818181818185,"ess":336.9016266460127,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Dubai</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Dubai rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, and its stated probabilities are honest throughout.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (16%), believe about\n<b>11%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 660 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-04. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 20.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.09, ranked 130 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(97&ndash;134) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>575</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">0 of 2 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Dubai</b> <span class=\"muted\">AE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">probabilities honest throughout</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.09</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>97&ndash;134\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>660 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Dubai &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Dubai\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.03078260869565,381.36695652173916 116.38917647058824,300.63529411764705 116.38917647058824,343.45882352941175 58.03078260869565,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"377.03636363636366\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"377.03636363636366\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.03078260869565,382.0 116.38917647058824,343.45882352941175\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 575 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.03078260869565\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"116.38917647058824\" cy=\"343.45882352941175\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(1%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Dubai the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.43) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.22).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'>-0.222</td><td class='num'>1.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>129</td><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'>0.433</td><td class='num'>0.2%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>0.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>0.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":25.07725,"lon":55.30927,"n":660,"n_cities":134,"name":"Dubai","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":8.695652173913044e-05,"n":575,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.16494117647058826,"n":85,"obs":0.10588235294117647,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":20.5,"provisional":false,"rank":130,"rank_hi":134.0,"rank_lo":97.0,"reliability":0.0004492115787026276,"resolution":0.0012578998541565385,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"dubai","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Dubai"}